  "id": "nominal-primitive-subtype-browser-ordinary-full-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "310f653c2bbc14178809eae23c4ae0bfea70cba1",
  "command": "EMCC_CORES='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_LAKE_RUNTIME_ROOT='/app/build/lean-link-spike/lazy' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_BROWSER_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_MODES='full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1469-browser-installed-ordinary-full-r1/selections' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_TYPE_CORPUS_BROWSERS='chromium,firefox,webkit' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH='/app/.toolchains/playwright' node '--max-old-space-size=3072' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nominal-primitive-subtype-npm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce both complete npm archives. Offline installation follows author removal; unchanged JavaScript and strict TypeScript callers replay after moving the installed tree. Source-free page, React and worker bundles then execute in all three engines, producing twelve browser executions and fifty-one lifecycle observations per selection. The full API checks per-site constructors, normalization, repeated record fields, active variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards, rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Primitive-base nominal browser acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Pages, React production/Strict Mode and dedicated workers execute in all three pinned Chromium, Firefox and WebKit engines on Linux x64 using wasm32 payloads. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete npm archives from two authors and install offline after author removal. Node and strict TypeScript callers replay after relocation; browser bundles run after installed sources are removed. All contexts check missing-asset recovery, with React remount and pending-unmount checks and worker restart/disposal. Complete Lean component/runtime archives, original records, selected producer sources, generator closure and runtime inputs are retained. External toolchain/browser binaries, framework archives and deployment bundles are not retained. Local compilation uses the recorded Nix command transport adapter, not a Nix sandbox. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted acceptance of later revisions; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
